Subject: is there any difference between these ways to specify priors
Message-ID: <7j1OPP3o1u4.VEi_hgmFYDUJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/7j1OPP3o1u4/m/VEi_hgmFYDUJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

beta0 below are regression coefficients. Does the difference among different prior specification have any impact on mixing or convergence?

#method 1

parameters {

    vector [100] beta0;

}

model {

beta0 ~ normal(0,32);

...

}

 # method 2

parameters {

    vector [100] beta0;

}

model {

for ( i in 1:100) beta0[i]~ normal(0,32);

...

}

 #method 3

parameters {

    vector [100] beta0;

}

transformed data {

            cov_matrix [100] sigma0;

            vector [100] z0;

            z0 <- rep_vector(0.0, 100);

            sigma0 <- diag_matrix( rep_vector(32^2, 100) );

}

model {

beta0 ~ multi_normal(z0,sigma0);

...

}

