That looks like a bug in the functions.  I'm afraid this
is going to hold up their release, though --- I need to
add some more tests to try to recreate this bug in our
unit tests for the function.

> May I make a wish?

Of course --- we have an issue tracker if you want to record
your wishes as feature requests.

> I think that functions that provide shorthand forms for common expressions, but are also much more efficient, are
> strongly needed.
> Replacing a plain matrix operation, such as D * L or D * Omega * D, with two for loops just because those plain
> operations are very inefficient, as you often say, is (boring and) error-prone.
> I hope that diag_pre_multiply() and diag_post_multiply() will soon be available and that something like
> diag_symmetric_diag_multiply() will follow.

We're working on them.  For every new function like this we
need double, reverse-mode auto-diff and forward-mode auto-diff
implementations.  Ideally, with the auto-diff specialized to
the function at hand.  They're easier to write if they're
just shorthand, but the diag_symmetric_diag could be made
much more efficient by not duplicating effort on the symmetric
calculations.

- Bob

