Yeah, I think a parameterization in terms of (K - 1) deltas is the right approach,
both in terms of computational efficiency and defining interpretable priors.
It also has the right relationship to a simplex (K - 1 translation-invariant deltas
exponentiate to K - 1 scale-invariant probabilities) -- this is the intuition for which
I was looking earlier.

